  "If bleeding continues past what is usual for you, the commonly cited limits are fifteen days for hayd and forty for nifas. Beyond them, the bleeding is generally treated as istihadha: pray, fast, and speak to a scholar and a doctor. Neither of them will find the question unusual.": "Kanama sizin i\xE7in al\u0131\u015F\u0131lagelenin \xF6tesinde s\xFCrerse, yayg\u0131n olarak zikredilen s\u0131n\u0131rlar hay\u0131z i\xE7in on be\u015F, nifas i\xE7in k\u0131rk g\xFCnd\xFCr. Bunlar\u0131n \xF6tesinde kanama genellikle istihaza say\u0131l\u0131r: namaz k\u0131l\u0131n, oru\xE7 tutun, bir \xE2limle ve bir doktorla konu\u015Fun. \u0130kisi de bu soruyu ola\u011Fand\u0131\u015F\u0131 bulmayacakt\u0131r.",
  "If bleeding stops before Fajr and the fast is intended that night, the fast stands. Ghusl is required before the prayer; it is not a condition of the fast itself. A woman may wake in a state that defers Fajr and still hold a valid fast.": "Kanama sabah namaz\u0131ndan \xF6nce kesilir ve o gece oruca niyet edilmi\u015Fse oru\xE7 ge\xE7erlidir. Gus\xFCl namazdan \xF6nce gerekir; orucun kendisi i\xE7in \u015Fart de\u011Fildir. Bir kad\u0131n sabah namaz\u0131n\u0131 erteleyen bir halde uyanabilir ve yine de ge\xE7erli bir oru\xE7 tutmu\u015F olur.",
  "If this changes, this page changes with it.": "Bu de\u011Fi\u015Firse, bu sayfa da onunla de\u011Fi\u015Fir.",
