  "Days fasted in each month, oldest first.": "S\u1ED1 ng\xE0y \u0111\xE3 nh\u1ECBn chay trong m\u1ED7i th\xE1ng, c\u0169 nh\u1EA5t tr\u01B0\u1EDBc.",
  "Days missed through hayd or nifas are made up one for one. There is no fidyah on them, because fidyah belongs to the one who cannot make the day up at all. A woman who can fast later fasts later.": "Nh\u1EEFng ng\xE0y b\u1ECF l\u1EE1 v\xEC hayd ho\u1EB7c nifas \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c b\xF9 theo t\u1EF7 l\u1EC7 m\u1ED9t \u0111\u1ED5i m\u1ED9t. Kh\xF4ng c\xF3 fidyah tr\xEAn ch\xFAng, v\xEC fidyah thu\u1ED9c v\u1EC1 ng\u01B0\u1EDDi kh\xF4ng th\u1EC3 b\xF9 ng\xE0y \u0111\xF3 ch\xFAt n\xE0o. Ng\u01B0\u1EDDi ph\u1EE5 n\u1EEF c\xF3 th\u1EC3 nh\u1ECBn chay b\xF9 sau n\xE0y th\xEC nh\u1ECBn chay b\xF9 sau n\xE0y.",
  "Days of Ramadan missed through menstruation or post-natal bleeding are made up before the next Ramadan, one day for each day. They do not need to be consecutive, and they may be spread through the year \u2014 but they are a debt, so most women keep a running count. This area records those days for you and keeps the scorecard honest as you settle them.": "Nh\u1EEFng ng\xE0y c\u1EE7a Ramadan b\u1ECB b\u1ECF l\u1EE1 v\xEC kinh nguy\u1EC7t ho\u1EB7c ra m\xE1u sau sinh \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c b\xF9 tr\u01B0\u1EDBc Ramadan ti\u1EBFp theo, m\u1ED7i ng\xE0y b\xF9 cho m\u1ED9t ng\xE0y. Ch\xFAng kh\xF4ng c\u1EA7n ph\u1EA3i li\xEAn ti\u1EBFp, v\xE0 c\xF3 th\u1EC3 r\u1EA3i ra trong n\u0103m \u2014 nh\u01B0ng \u0111\xF3 l\xE0 m\u1ED9t m\xF3n n\u1EE3, n\xEAn h\u1EA7u h\u1EBFt ph\u1EE5 n\u1EEF gi\u1EEF m\u1ED9t s\u1ED1 \u0111\u1EBFm li\xEAn t\u1EE5c. Khu v\u1EF1c n\xE0y ghi l\u1EA1i nh\u1EEFng ng\xE0y \u0111\xF3 cho b\u1EA1n v\xE0 gi\u1EEF cho b\u1EA3ng \u0111i\u1EC3m lu\xF4n trung th\u1EF1c khi b\u1EA1n x\u1EED l\xFD ch\xFAng.",
