  "If bleeding continues past what is usual for you, the commonly cited limits are fifteen days for hayd and forty for nifas. Beyond them, the bleeding is generally treated as istihadha: pray, fast, and speak to a scholar and a doctor. Neither of them will find the question unusual.": "N\u1EBFu vi\u1EC7c ra m\xE1u ti\u1EBFp di\u1EC5n v\u01B0\u1EE3t qu\xE1 m\u1EE9c b\xECnh th\u01B0\u1EDDng c\u1EE7a b\u1EA1n, c\xE1c gi\u1EDBi h\u1EA1n th\u01B0\u1EDDng \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c tr\xEDch d\u1EABn l\xE0 m\u01B0\u1EDDi l\u0103m ng\xE0y \u0111\u1ED1i v\u1EDBi hayd v\xE0 b\u1ED1n m\u01B0\u01A1i ng\xE0y \u0111\u1ED1i v\u1EDBi nifas. V\u01B0\u1EE3t qu\xE1 ch\xFAng, vi\u1EC7c ra m\xE1u th\u01B0\u1EDDng \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c coi l\xE0 istihadha: h\xE3y c\u1EA7u nguy\u1EC7n, nh\u1ECBn chay, v\xE0 trao \u0111\u1ED5i v\u1EDBi m\u1ED9t h\u1ECDc gi\u1EA3 v\xE0 m\u1ED9t b\xE1c s\u0129. C\u1EA3 hai \u0111\u1EC1u s\u1EBD th\u1EA5y c\xE2u h\u1ECFi n\xE0y kh\xF4ng c\xF3 g\xEC l\u1EA1.",
  "If bleeding stops before Fajr and the fast is intended that night, the fast stands. Ghusl is required before the prayer; it is not a condition of the fast itself. A woman may wake in a state that defers Fajr and still hold a valid fast.": "N\u1EBFu vi\u1EC7c ra m\xE1u d\u1EEBng l\u1EA1i tr\u01B0\u1EDBc Fajr v\xE0 ng\xE0y chay \u0111\xE3 \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c l\u1EADp niyyah v\xE0o \u0111\xEAm \u0111\xF3, th\xEC ng\xE0y chay \u1EA5y c\xF3 gi\xE1 tr\u1ECB. L\u1EC5 ghusl l\xE0 b\u1EAFt bu\u1ED9c tr\u01B0\u1EDBc l\u1EC5 nguy\u1EC7n; n\xF3 kh\xF4ng ph\u1EA3i l\xE0 \u0111i\u1EC1u ki\u1EC7n c\u1EE7a ch\xEDnh vi\u1EC7c nh\u1ECBn chay. M\u1ED9t ng\u01B0\u1EDDi ph\u1EE5 n\u1EEF c\xF3 th\u1EC3 th\u1EE9c d\u1EADy trong m\u1ED9t t\xECnh tr\u1EA1ng khi\u1EBFn l\u1EC5 Fajr b\u1ECB ho\xE3n m\xE0 v\u1EABn gi\u1EEF \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c m\u1ED9t ng\xE0y chay h\u1EE3p l\u1EC7.",
  "If this changes, this page changes with it.": "N\u1EBFu \u0111i\u1EC1u n\xE0y thay \u0111\u1ED5i, trang n\xE0y c\u0169ng thay \u0111\u1ED5i theo.",
