  "Names": "C\xE1c t\xEAn",
  'Narrated Anas bin Malik:The Prophet (\uFDFA) said, "Take Suhur as there is a blessing in it': 'Do Anas bin Malik thu\u1EADt l\u1EA1i: Thi\xEAn S\u1EE9 \uFDFA n\xF3i: "H\xE3y d\xF9ng b\u1EEFa Suhur, v\xEC trong \u0111\xF3 c\xF3 m\u1ED9t s\u1EF1 ph\xFAc l\xE0nh',
  'Narrated Talha bin `Abdullah bin `Auf:I offered the funeral prayer behind Ibn `Abbas and he recited Al-Fatiha and said, "You should know that it (i.e. recitation of Al-Fatiha) is the tradition of the Prophet Muhammad (\uFDFA)': 'Do Talha bin `Abdullah bin `Auf thu\u1EADt l\u1EA1i: T\xF4i \u0111\xE3 d\xE2ng l\u1EC5 nguy\u1EC7n tang l\u1EC5 ph\xEDa sau Ibn `Abbas v\xE0 \xF4ng \u0111\xE3 \u0111\u1ECDc Al-Fatiha v\xE0 n\xF3i: "C\xE1c b\u1EA1n n\xEAn bi\u1EBFt r\u1EB1ng vi\u1EC7c \u0111\xF3 (t\u1EE9c vi\u1EC7c \u0111\u1ECDc Al-Fatiha) l\xE0 Sunnah c\u1EE7a Thi\xEAn S\u1EE9 Muhammad \uFDFA"',
  "Narrator": "Ng\u01B0\u1EDDi truy\u1EC1n thu\u1EADt",
  "Naskh": "Naskh",
  "Natural bleeding that comes to a woman at its known time, without a cause such as injury or illness. Commonly cited limits are a minimum of three days and a maximum of fifteen, with at least fifteen days of purity between two cycles. Anything outside that pattern is usually treated as istihadha, and the details belong with a scholar.": "Ra m\xE1u t\u1EF1 nhi\xEAn \u0111\u1EBFn v\u1EDBi ng\u01B0\u1EDDi ph\u1EE5 n\u1EEF v\xE0o th\u1EDDi \u0111i\u1EC3m \u0111\xE3 bi\u1EBFt c\u1EE7a n\xF3, kh\xF4ng c\xF3 nguy\xEAn nh\xE2n nh\u01B0 ch\u1EA5n th\u01B0\u01A1ng hay b\u1EC7nh t\u1EADt. C\xE1c gi\u1EDBi h\u1EA1n th\u01B0\u1EDDng \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c tr\xEDch d\u1EABn l\xE0 t\u1ED1i thi\u1EC3u ba ng\xE0y v\xE0 t\u1ED1i \u0111a m\u01B0\u1EDDi l\u0103m ng\xE0y, v\u1EDBi \xEDt nh\u1EA5t m\u01B0\u1EDDi l\u0103m ng\xE0y thanh s\u1EA1ch gi\u1EEFa hai chu k\u1EF3. B\u1EA5t c\u1EE9 \u0111i\u1EC1u g\xEC n\u1EB1m ngo\xE0i m\u1EABu h\xECnh \u0111\xF3 th\u01B0\u1EDDng \u0111\u01B0\u1EE3c coi l\xE0 istihadha, v\xE0 c\xE1c chi ti\u1EBFt thu\u1ED9c v\u1EC1 m\u1ED9t h\u1ECDc gi\u1EA3.",
